   <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\">Not Showcasing Your Product Or Showing Your Product Too Much In Your Social Media Video Production</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>A common mistake is either focusing solely on your product or never showing it at all. Your product should be integrated naturally within a story or context that shows why it's helpful. Avoid overly salesy videos, instead, demonstrate value and solve problems for your audience. This approach feels genuine and keeps viewers interested. On the other hand some people hate selling so much that they never do it and so their audience won't even know what they sell. You can keep a balance by thinking about the three different types of content: growth, nurture and sales. I think&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.instagram.com/rudyjude/\" class=\"text-info\">Julie D. O'Rourke's instagram </a>account is the perfect example of this.<br></p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
