v class=\"title col-12 col-md-8\">\n                <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\">2. How to Edit Videos for Social Media: Rough Cut &amp; Story Structure</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>When learning how to edit <a href=\"social-media-video-ideas.html\" class=\"text-info\">videos for social media</a>, start simple. Lay down your main audio or voice track first, then build from there:<br>Cut, cut, cut: Cut out “ums,” long pauses, or anything that slows the story down.<br>Pick the <a href=\"video-advice-composition.html\" class=\"text-info\">best B-roll</a>: Use shots that really support what you’re saying.<br>Stick to your story: Keep the arc clear — Hook → Challenge → Build → Resolution.<br>Think of the rough cut as the skeleton of your video. Once it’s in place, everything else, pacing, music, and polishing becomes way easier.<br></p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
