v class=\"title col-12 col-md-8\">\n                <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\">3. Pacing &amp; Contrast</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>Understanding how to edit videos for social media isn’t just about cutting footage it’s about rhythm and energy:<br>Mix slow and fast shots: slow for emphasis, fast for excitement.<br>Add contrast: slow → fast, quiet → loud, wide → close-up, bright → dark.<br>Only include shots that serve the story.<br>Let the audience fill in gaps naturally (Kuleshov effect).<br>Use open loops to keep viewers curious - leave a hint of what’s coming next or a mini cliffhanger before a cut. This makes your audience want to keep watching, and you can close the loop later in the video.<br>Rhythm is critical in editing videos for social media that keep viewers watching until the end.<br></p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
