   <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\">4. How to Edit Videos for Social Media: Music &amp; Sound Transitions</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>When learning how to edit videos for social media, it’s all about using it to support your story, not distract from it.<br>Add music after your rough cut: Let your story guide the soundtrack.<br>Match the energy: Each section of your video should have music that fits the mood.<br>Switching music between sections:<br>Smooth fade: Gradually lower the old track while bringing in the new one.<br>Impact sound: A whoosh, pop, or drum hit can signal a transition.<br>Use J-cuts &amp; L-cuts: Start the next scene’s audio early (J-Cut) or let the current audio flow into the next shot (L-Cut).<br>Keep it under dialogue: Music should enhance your message, not overpower it.<br>The right music and sound make your video feel polished, professional, and fun, it’s a big part of how to edit videos for social media.</p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
