v class=\"title col-12 col-md-8\">\n                <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-7\">The Problem (Pain Points)</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>The real reason your videos aren't driving continuous donations isn't a lack of donor empathy or a bad mission statement. It’s the \"One-and-Done\" Gala Trap combined with standard commercial videographers who don't understand trauma-informed storytelling. Traditional creators focus strictly on hyper-stylized aesthetic choices. They lack the editorial patience to build real rapport with vulnerable communities, and they leave you with a massive, uncompressed video link that sits gathering dust on an unoptimized YouTube channel.<br><br>If you don't fix this now, you will keep wasting your strictly monitored budget on disjointed content that triggers consumer skepticism or looks like superficial \"greenwashing.\" Your internal team will continue to face burnout acting as impromptu production fixers, crowd controllers, and script supervisors. Meanwhile, your competitors and peers will continue to capture the digital narrative, secure critical grant applications, and lock in recurring monthly donors.<br></p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LI