v class=\"title col-12 col-md-8\">\n                <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\"></h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>Planning a corporate event, launching a fresh brand campaign, or organizing a commercial shoot is an exciting process, and you are likely dreaming about how amazing that final film is going to look. As you dive into the details, you might find yourself wondering about a very common industry question: Do videographers give you RAW footage? To give you the short answer right away: no, most professional videographers do not give you RAW footage by default.Think of it less as a rigid rule and more like a standard creative partnership. If you happen to need the unedited, original files from your video shoot, it is simply a matter of chatting about it upfront, adding a few specific details to your contract, and planning for an extra fee. Taking a quick look behind the scenes at how production teams work is the easiest way to keep your project stress-free and ensure your business walks away with the exact assets you need!<br><br></p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
