v class=\"title col-12 col-md-8\">\n                <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\">What Exactly Is RAW Video Footage?</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>To understand why professionals protect these files, you first need to know what they actually are. RAW footage is not simply an \"unedited video clip.\" It is the completely unaltered, uncompressed data captured directly by a digital camera sensor.<br>When you look at a RAW video file on a monitor, it looks terrible. The image is flat, gray, washed out, and lacks contrast. Camera manufacturers like RED, Sony, and Blackmagic design files this way on purpose. By preserving all the original light and color data, the file gives editors the maximum amount of flexibility during the post-production process.<br>Transforming those flat files into a cinematic masterpiece requires extensive work. A professional editor must handle color correction, creative color grading, sound design, audio balancing, and pacing. Without this technical work, the footage is practically unusable for the average consumer.</p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
