v class=\"title col-12 col-md-8\">\n                <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\">Why Most Professionals Do Not Share Unedited Files</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>If you ask your production team for these files, do not be surprised if they decline or charge a premium. Videographers guard their unedited media for several specific professional and technical reasons.<br><br>The Work is Incomplete<br>Think of a videographer as a chef or an author. A chef does not serve you raw ingredients, and an author does not publish their first rough draft. To a professional filmmaker, RAW files represent an incomplete piece of art. The magic happens during the creative editing process. Delivering an unfinished product goes against their professional standards.<br><br>Protecting the Brand and Reputation<br>If a client posts unedited, flat, or shaky clips on social media and tags the production company, it can damage the filmmaker's reputation. Potential clients might see the washed-out colors or unmixed audio and assume the videographer does not know how to handle a camera. Professionals protect their brand by ensuring only polished, finished work enters the public eye.<br><br>Technical Barriers and Massive File Sizes<br>RAW video files are completely different from smartphone video clips. They are absolutely massive. A single hour of high-resolution RAW footage can easily take up hundreds of gigabytes of storage space. Most everyday laptops cannot even playback these files smoothly without lagging. You need specialized editing software like DaVinci Resolve or Premiere Pro, along with a powerful computer, just to open them.<br></p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
