v class=\"title col-12 col-md-8\">\n                <h2 mbr-if=\"showTitle\" class=\"align-center mbr-bold mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\"><br>Smart Alternatives to RAW Footage</h2>\n                <h3 mbr-if=\"showSubtitle\" class=\"mbr-section-subtitle align-center mbr-light mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-section-subtitle\">Bringing Your Brand to Life Through Video</h3>\n                <p class=\"mbr-text align-center mbr-white pb-3 mbr-fonts-style\" mbr-theme-style=\"display-5\" data-app-selector=\".mbr-text\" mbr-if=\"showText\" mbr-article data-multiline>If you just want to make sure you do not miss any behind-the-scenes clips, extra angles, or unedited moments, you probably do not actually need RAW data. Ask your production team for one of these common alternatives instead:<br>* A B-Roll Reel: A long compilation of extra background footage and ambient shots. These clips are usually color-graded and cleaned up, making them perfect for quick social media posts.<br>* A Documentary Edit: This is a long-form video package that shows full sequences—like an entire corporate presentation, a complete interview, or project milestones—edited sequentially with clean audio and color.<br>* ProRes or Linear Exports: If you plan to hire a separate editor later, ask for high-quality, edited ProRes files instead of RAW. This gives your future editor clean, professional assets to work with immediately.<br></p>\n                <div class=\"mbr-section-btn align-center\" mbr-if=\"showButtons\" mbr-buttons mbr-theme-style=\"display-4\" data-toolbar=\"-mbrBtnMove\">\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-primary\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LEARN MORE</a>\n                    <a class=\"btn btn-white-outline\" href=\"https://mobirise.co\">LIVE DEMO</a>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</section>",
